On Fri, Jun 21, 2013 at 3:16 PM, <frie...@gene.com> wrote:

>
> Inside apache prefork (at least my setup!) sending a worker process the SIGUSR1 signal does exactly what I am asking---it tells the process to continue serving the current request and then kill itself. It takes another minute or so to die after but it works. The parent process will then spin off a new process.

I have never used SIGUSR, but from what I read it is a custom defined signal that doesn't do anything by default? I am not sure how it results in the behavior you describe.

Forking in R is easy using the parallel package which ships with r-base. Look into ?mcparallel and ?mccollect if you don't want to install the RAppArmor package.

